Z||000037||Gold-86SE||02-17-2001||01:38 AM||||<BR>Ok, so it is not exactly a movie, but a big show none-the-less.<P>Miami Vice - First Season (84-85)<BR>Episode 19 - "The Home Invaders"<BR>Original Air Date - 15 Mar 1985 (NBC)<P>Description:<BR>The Fiero is Red, has Hi-Tech Turbo wheels, and luggage rack, and is most likely an 84 model. Being that the rear deck is not visible, I made a best guess based on the original air date of the show.<P>The Scene:<BR>We see the Fiero at about 40 minutes after the hour.  Prior to the Fiero scene, the Miami police have a couple of hookers identify the suspect in the portfolio of criminals, then drive the hookers up to a business to confirm the id.  As they drive into the parking space, behind them you will see the Passenger side of the Fiero, starting at the rear of the door.<P>It was pretty cool, been watching for it, and was finally rewarded.||||reg||1
