Z||000046||My7Fieros||02-19-2001||01:54 PM||||Ok Ive got one nobodys mentioned yet....<BR>My g/f was watching a Lifetime movie (EEEKKK!!!) about the Texas mother who wanted her friend killed because of thier rival daughters cheerleading compitition (true story). I actually started watching it (dont say a word!) and theres a scene where the mother (Leslie Ann Warren) and her daughter get into their Lincoln at the high school and theres a red coupe parked next to them. Good shot of it to, you can see it when they get in the car, then when they drive off you can see it clear as day (even though it was night in the scene). Red 84-86 coupe. <BR>...The only good thing Ive ever seen on Lifetime lol......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000047||fiero56||04-04-2001||08:17 PM||||I know a lot of people were having trouble spotting the red coupe in <I>Gone In Sixty Seconds</I> before. Well, I found a better shot of it. <P>On the DVD if you go to the Bonus Materials section or something like that, click on the part where they mention making the jump scene. The coupe is very visible. The shot is taken from the Helicopters point of view way above the bridge right at the accident. It has some Blue GM car on top of it. Not really though, CGI. I can dig up the frame numbers if needed. Of course, I'll have to suffer more grueling time watching that very poorly produced movie <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Actually, its one of my favorites.||||reg||1
